### Upload file to Blob store

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/cli/blob

Uploads a file to the Blob store with specified access level.

```bash
vercel blob put [path-to-file] --access private
```

--------------------------------

### Upload Files from the Browser using Presigned URLs

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob/vercel-signed-urls

Uses the uploadPresigned function to stream files directly to Blob storage without exposing authorization headers. Requires the handleUploadUrl to point to your server-side route handler.

```tsx
'use client';

import { uploadPresigned, type PutBlobResult } from '@vercel/blob/client';
import { useRef, useState } from 'react';

export default function UploadPage(): React.JSX.Element {
  const inputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);
  const [blob, setBlob] = useState<PutBlobResult | null>(null);

  return (
    <form
      onSubmit={async (event) => {
        event.preventDefault();
        const file = inputRef.current?.files?.[0];
        if (!file) return;

        const result = await uploadPresigned(file.name, file, {
          access: 'private',
          handleUploadUrl: '/api/upload-presigned',
        });
        setBlob(result);
      }}
    >
      <input ref={inputRef} type="file" />
      <button type="submit">Upload</button>
      {blob ? <a href={blob.url}>{blob.url}</a> : null}
    </form>
  );
}
```

--------------------------------

### Upload files to blob storage

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob/manage-blob-storage

Commands for uploading files with various configurations like content types, cache control, and overwrite permissions.

```bash
vercel blob put ./assets/logo.png --pathname images/logo.png --access public
```

```bash
vercel blob put ./data/config.json --content-type application/json --access public
```

```bash
vercel blob put ./assets/hero.jpg --pathname images/hero.jpg --cache-control-max-age 86400 --access public
```

```bash
vercel blob put ./assets/logo-v2.png --pathname images/logo.png --allow-overwrite --access public
```

```bash
vercel blob put ./uploads/photo.jpg --add-random-suffix --access private
```

--------------------------------

### upload(pathname, body, options)

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob/using-blob-sdk

Uploads a file directly from the client to the Vercel Blob store. It coordinates with a server-side route to obtain a secure token before performing the upload.

```APIDOC
## upload(pathname, body, options)

### Description
Uploads a file directly from the client (like a browser) to the Vercel Blob store. It fetches a client token on your server using the `handleUploadUrl` before performing the actual upload.

### Parameters
- **pathname** (string) - Required - A string specifying the base value of the return URL.
- **body** (ReadableStream | String | ArrayBuffer | Blob) - Required - The file content to upload.
- **options** (object) - Required - Configuration for the upload.
  - **access** ('private' | 'public') - Required - Determines the access level of the blob.
  - **handleUploadUrl** (string) - Required - A string specifying the route to call for generating client tokens.
  - **contentType** (string) - Optional - A string indicating the media type. By default, it's extracted from the pathname's extension.
  - **clientPayload** (string) - Optional - A string to be sent to your `handleUpload` server code.
  - **multipart** (boolean) - Optional - Pass `true` when uploading large files to split the file into multiple parts.
  - **abortSignal** (AbortSignal) - Optional - An AbortSignal to cancel the operation.
  - **onUploadProgress** (function) - Optional - Callback to track upload progress: `onUploadProgress({loaded: number, total: number, percentage: number})`.

### Response
Returns a `JSON` object with the following data for the created blob object:
- **pathname** (string) - The path of the uploaded blob.
- **contentType** (string) - The media type of the blob.
- **contentDisposition** (string) - The content disposition header value.
- **url** (string) - The URL of the uploaded blob.
- **downloadUrl** (string) - The URL for downloading the blob.
- **etag** (string) - The entity tag for the blob.

### Response Example
{
  "pathname": "profilesv1/user-12345.txt",
  "contentType": "text/plain",
  "contentDisposition": "inline; filename=\"user-12345.txt\"",
  "url": "https://ce0rcu23vrrdzqap.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/profilesv1/REDACTED.txt",
  "downloadUrl": "https://ce0rcu23vrrdzqap.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/profilesv1/REDACTED.txt?download=1",
  "etag": "\"5f7d8e...\""
}
```

--------------------------------

### Upload a file to public storage

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob/public-storage

Use the put function with access set to public to store files in a public Blob store.

```ts
import { put } from '@vercel/blob';

export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const form = await request.formData();
  const file = form.get('file') as File;

  const blob = await put(file.name, file, {
    access: 'public',
  });

  return Response.json(blob);
}
```

--------------------------------

### Upload a blob using PUT presigned URLs in TypeScript

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob/vercel-signed-urls

Generate one-off upload URLs with specific constraints like content types and size limits. Use ifMatch to ensure the upload only succeeds if the blob hasn't changed.

```ts
import { head, issueSignedToken, presignUrl } from '@vercel/blob';

const { etag } = await head(
  'https://<storeId>.private.blob.vercel-storage.com/media/photo.png',
);

const token = await issueSignedToken({
  pathname: 'media/photo.png',
  operations: ['put'],
  allowedContentTypes: ['image/png'],
  maximumSizeInBytes: 10 * 1024 * 1024,
  validUntil: Date.now() + 60 * 60 * 1000,
});

const { presignedUrl } = await presignUrl(token, {
  operation: 'put',
  pathname: 'media/photo.png',
  access: 'private',
  allowedContentTypes: ['image/png'],
  maximumSizeInBytes: 10 * 1024 * 1024,
  addRandomSuffix: false,
  allowOverwrite: true,
  ifMatch: etag,
});

const res = await fetch(presignedUrl, {
  method: 'PUT',
  headers: { 'content-type': 'image/png' },
  body: pngBytes,
});
```

--------------------------------

### Client-Side Upload in Next.js Pages Router

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob/client-upload

Implements a file upload form using the Vercel Blob client SDK within a Next.js Pages Router component.

```tsx
import { type PutBlobResult } from '@vercel/blob';
import { upload } from '@vercel/blob/client';
import { useState, useRef } from 'react';

export default function AvatarUploadPage() {
  const inputFileRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);
  const [blob, setBlob] = useState<PutBlobResult | null>(null);
  return (
    <>
      <h1>Upload Your Avatar</h1>

      <form
        onSubmit={async (event) => {
          event.preventDefault();

          if (!inputFileRef.current?.files) {
            throw new Error('No file selected');
          }

          const file = inputFileRef.current.files[0];

          const newBlob = await upload(file.name, file, {
            access: 'private' /* or 'public' */,
            handleUploadUrl: '/api/avatar/upload',
          });

          setBlob(newBlob);
        }}
      >
        <input
          name="file"
          ref={inputFileRef}
          type="file"
          accept="image/jpeg, image/png, image/webp"
          required
        />
        <button type="submit">Upload</button>
      </form>
      {blob && (
        <div>
          Blob url: <a href={blob.url}>{blob.url}</a>
        </div>
      )}
    </>
  );
}
```

